			"date": "2025-02-19T06:21:23.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> <span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://writing.exchange/@matt\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>matt</span></a></span> Is there a way this might be integrated into Write Freely or Write.as? I tried adding it to my individual posts, but I think the Meta tag gets scrubbed from the editor in Write Freely.... Might be related to the markdown compiler dependency that you use?? FWIW, I don't care how it gets embedded into the content, I would just love if Write.as would allow me to set a meta tag with name and content attributes. What do you think?</p>",
